🐘 PostgreSQL Learning Notes (Practical SQL)Welcome to my PostgreSQL practice repository! This guide summarizes key concepts, SQL syntax, and database techniques learned from Practical SQL.📊 Summary of Topics LearnedSectionTopicCore Concepts & HighlightsKey Syntax / Functions01. FundamentalsTables & Basic QueriesTable creation, row insertion, filtering, sorting, and pattern matching.SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIKE, ILIKE02. Data TypesText, Numeric, Date & JSON• Text: char(n) (fixed), varchar(n) (variable), text (unlimited)• Numeric: smallint, integer, bigint, serial, decimal• Date/Time: timestamp, date, time, interval• JSON vs JSONB: Key-value format vs. optimized binary storage• Type Casting: Converting data typesCAST(col AS type), col::type03. Data TransferImporting & ExportingLoading external CSV files into tables and exporting table data or selected sub-columns.COPY table FROM 'path' WITH (FORMAT CSV, DELIMITER ',')COPY table TO 'path' WITH (FORMAT CSV, DELIMITER ',')04. Math & StatsBasic Math & Summary StatsArithmetic operations following BODMAS, basic descriptive statistics, and percentile calculations.+, -, *, /, %, ^, |/, ||/avg(), mode(), percentile_cont()05. RelationshipsJoins & Table Relations• Join Types: Inner, Left, Right, Full Outer, Cross• Cardinality: One-to-One, One-to-Many, Many-to-ManyINNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN, FULL OUTER JOIN, CROSS JOIN06. Best PracticesNaming IdentifiersClean database conventions: snake_case, plural table names, descriptive aliases, avoiding cryptic abbreviations.e.g., country_name, australian_states07. Data IntegrityConstraints & Indexing• Primary Keys: Natural, Surrogate, Composite• Foreign Keys: Enforcing relations & cascading deletes• Rules: CHECK, UNIQUE, NOT NULL• Indexing: Query optimizationPRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY ... ON DELETE CASCADE, CHECK(), UNIQUE, NOT NULL, CREATE INDEX08. AggregationsAggregates & GroupingGrouping rows to perform calculations across datasets.GROUP BY, COUNT(), MIN(), MAX(), SUM()09. MaintenanceTable Modification & Safety• Inspecting NULL values and inconsistencies• Altering or dropping structures• Safeguarding work via backup tables• Transaction managementALTER TABLE, DROP TABLE, BEGIN, COMMIT, ROLLBACK10. AnalyticsAdvanced Stats & WindowsAnalytical calculations and row ranking without collapsing datasets.Correlation, linear regression functions, RANK() OVER (), DENSE_RANK() OVER ()
